{
  "dom_id": "step-q96960",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.015.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.965$ | $0.970$ | $0.975$ | $0.980$ | $0.985$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.8119\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.0537\\,$ | $\\,2.1701\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.1701)=0.985.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.1701)=1-0.985=0.015.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.1701)=0.015.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165008/assets/47a123a730cf175bea1d1887ffdc5a9feb3e1d8f07208c28a9f893a9a1688005.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.1701) & =0.015 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.1701) & =0.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.1701.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
